      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has many unused imports, constants, and helper methods that clutter the single `test_plus` test. I'll produce a clean version that:\n1. Removes all unused imports, constants, and data provider methods\n2. Formats the `data_plus` table with a header comment explaining each column\n3. Uses clearer row-level grouping with blank linesNow let me compile-check the file.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored file removes all unused imports, constants, and helper methods (leaving only `SECS_PER_DAY`, `NANOS_PER_SEC`, and `NANOS_PER_DAY`), adds a Javadoc table explaining each column of the parameterized data, and formats the `data_plus` rows into labelled groups so readers can immediately understand what scenario each block exercises."
